  "title": "Great Trigonometrical Survey",
  "summary": "The Great Trigonometrical Survey of India began in 1802 under William Lambton, who proposed mapping the subcontinent with triangles, starting from a baseline near Madras. George Everest took over after Lambton died in 1823. Its network later supported the measurement of Peak XV, officially announced in March 1856 as 29,002 ft.",
